 "summary": "Sikkim did not join India in 1947. India took over its administration during unrest in 1949, and under the treaty of 5 December 1950 the kingdom became an Indian protectorate: India ran its defence and foreign affairs, the Chogyal ruled at home. After the 1975 referendum Sikkim became India's 22nd state on 16 May 1975. The outline is the one the princely-states layer draws for British times; Sikkim's borders did not change.",
